{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["The reason for <b>unto Laban the Aramean</b> is to declare that even though he is an Aramean and the people of his place are men of teraphim and soothsayers like the Philistines (Isaiah 2:6), a prophetic dream came to him for the honor of the righteous one. And likewise, \"And Jacob stole the heart of Laban the Aramean\" — even though he is the Aramean who practices divination, the master of the teraphim." "<b>from good to evil</b> — all the good of the wicked is evil to the righteous, in the language of Rashi. And its plain sense: Guard yourself lest you speak with him to do him good if he returns with you from his way, or lest you frighten him into doing him evil if he does not come with you, for I have commanded him to return to his land."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:38:06.145819147Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}